{"skill":{"slug":"skill-finder-cn","displayName":"Skill Finder Cn"},"version":{"version":"1.0.1","createdAt":1774147904255,"changelog":"安装验证、搜索结果优化、中文输出","changelogSource":"user","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":2684,"sha256":"762005fbdc05a618726f663d4f0c70d7cbdd13c09339bd32475dc0debc9d0a46","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"_meta.json","size":134,"sha256":"462530538a9b5f3979809f68d15e4550a34f61271b627fc1729d301e3f547085","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"package.json","size":108,"sha256":"9245c1c9472bc37d6ad55ac2f50c4c636320c9f3afc23bb95bec65a31b9f46da","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"scripts/search.sh","size":262,"sha256":"47d7986b5d6163944af5e7ae656eba6446da671c4adb13fe1c98ef1b44cddda2","contentType":"application/x-sh"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2053,"sha256":"f95cb75163fbd9e27a5bb6c833fe78c9c3681029749bad27938d5b66f15fac70","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789070992977,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"532df313416731759d720a050ee01450397e730460c97f70894cb93076312803","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/532df313416731759d720a050ee01450397e730460c97f70894cb93076312803","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: skill-finder-cn\nVersion: 1.0.1\n\nThe skill-finder-cn bundle is a legitimate utility designed to help users search for and install skills from the ClawHub repository. It uses standard CLI commands (clawhub search/install), performs basic file system checks to verify installations within the expected workspace directory (~/.openclaw/workspace/skills/), and queries the official API (clawhub.ai) for statistics. No evidence of data exfiltration, malicious execution, or prompt injection was found.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779164794465},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":29,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":5,"checkedAt":1789070992977},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is a straightforward Chinese-language helper for finding and installing ClawHub skills, with no hidden persistence, credential handling, or destructive behavior found.","dimensions":[{"detail":"It uses ClawHub search/inspect/install, a ClawHub API stats query, and local checks under ~/.openclaw/workspace/skills; these are proportionate for a skill discovery and installation helper.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The package declares a dependency on the clawhub binary and includes a small search wrapper script; it does not add external dependencies or remote executable payloads.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"Activation examples are somewhat broad, but they are still framed around users asking for skills, and install actions are shown as explicit commands rather than hidden automation.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No background workers, startup hooks, privilege escalation, credential access, or cross-session persistence beyond user-directed skill installation were found.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is to search, inspect, recommend, install, and verify ClawHub skills; the listed commands all support that purpose.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install this if you want a Chinese-language ClawHub skill finder. Review recommendations before running any clawhub install command, because installing third-party skills can change what your agent is able to do.","findings":"[SQP-1] expected: The broad trigger language is a quality concern, but it is still connected to explicit skill-finding requests and does not by itself create hidden or unsafe behavior.\n[AS3] expected: The artifact suggests listing installed skills and checking for a specific installed SKILL.md file to verify installation; it does not instruct reading peer skill contents or extracting their instructions.\n[SQP-3] expected: Chinese-only user-facing text is clearly reflected by the CN name and Chinese description, and is a localization/usability note rather than a security concern.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789070992977}}}}}